  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 957 PM MDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nUpper high pressure will start to elongate Monday, stretching from\nSoCal to NM. High pressure will continue to meander over this \nsame area through around Wednesday allowing for the return of hot, \ntriple digit temperatures across the lowlands Monday through \nWednesday. Tuesday looks the hottest where Heat Advisories may be \nneeded for the Lower Valley and potentially El Paso. Continued \nstorm chances each day with a focus over the Gila region and \nwestern locations of the CWA bordering AZ. We may need to keep an\neye on the Lordsburg Playa these next few days if any storms are\nexpected to pop up nearby there. High pressure will still \ncontinue to influence the area Thursday and Friday but will \ngradually shift closer to NV/UT/AZ borders. Looks like it could be\na little more active with thunderstorm activity by the end of the\nwork week if we can get a better tap of moisture into the area. \nNot quite as hot Thu/Fri and into the weekend. Upper 90s and some \nfew triple digit readings expected during that time frame.",
